  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "libX11 security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for libX11 is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "Core X11 protocol client library.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA malicious X server could exploit a buffer overflow in libX11 before 1.8.14 during handling of XkbGetMap overflowing the key_sym_map.(CVE-2026-88806)\n\nAn out-of-bounds read vulnerability in libX11's XIM (X Input Method) attribute parser in libX11 before 1.8.14 could be used by malicious X servers to crash attached X clients.(CVE-2026-94283)\n\nAn out-of-bounds read vulnerability in libX11's XIM trigger-key registration parser in libX11 before 1.8.14 could be used by malicious X servers to crash attached X clients.(CVE-2026-94284)\n\nAn out-of-bounds read in libX11's byte-oriented codeset parser in libX11 before 1.8.14 could be used by malicious X servers to crash attached X clients.(CVE-2026-94285)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for libX11 is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of high. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "High",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "libX11",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
